          "text": "All 18 tests pass, including the ones marked `#[ignore]`.\n\nImplementation in `src/lib.rs`:\n\n- `lowest_price` counts copies of each of the five titles, sorts the counts in descending order, and hands them to a memoized recursive search.\n- `min_price` builds the basket one group at a time: at each step it tries every group size `k` from 1 to 5, taking one copy from the `k` most plentiful remaining titles, re-sorts the counts, and keeps the cheapest total. Because the counts are kept sorted, the state space is small and memoization makes it fast.\n- `group_cost` encodes the discount schedule in cents: 1→800, 2→1520 (5%), 3→2160 (10%), 4→2560 (20%), 5→3000 (25%).\n\nThe sorted-counts DP is optimal for this problem: any optimal grouping can be rearranged so each group draws from the most plentiful remaining titles, which is why the search only needs to choose the group size, not which specific titles."
